

Observability Lab: Dynatrace Grail & DQL Event Querying
1. Objective & Grail Lakehouse Overview
Dynatrace Grail is a schema-on-read data lakehouse designed to store and analyze observability data such as logs, metrics, events, and traces at scale.

Dynatrace Query Language (DQL) uses pipeline-based processing. Commands are connected using the pipe (|) operator. In this analysis:

fetch retrieves log records.
filter isolates required events.
summarize aggregates matching records.
sort orders the results for easier analysis.
The supplied Grail dataset contains 8 log records.

2. Formulating DQL Queries (fetch, filter, summarize, sort)
A. Filter Error Logs by Service
DQL Statement:
fetch logs
| filter status == "ERROR"
| summarize error_count = count(), by:{service.name, host.name}
| sort error_count desc
Observed Results:
Service Name	Host Name	Error Count
order-service	k8s-worker-node-02	3
payment-service	k8s-worker-node-03	1
Finding: There are 4 ERROR events in total. Three of the four ERROR events occur in order-service on k8s-worker-node-02, representing 75% of all ERROR events.

B. Grouping by Event Type & Time Bins
DQL Statement:
fetch logs
| filter status == "ERROR" or status == "WARN"
| summarize total_occurrences = count(), by:{event.type}
| sort total_occurrences desc
Event Breakdown:
Event Type	Total Occurrences
app_crash	3
network_timeout	1
performance_warning	1
retry	1
The remaining two records are INFO/audit events.

